<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto, Prince of Stolberg-Wernigerode</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837–1896</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Otto of Stolberg-Wernigerode</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto, Prince of Stolberg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wernigerode">Wernigerode</a>, was a German statesman and head of his family's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a> lands. He served as Oberpräsident of the Prussian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/province-of-hanover">Province of Hanover</a> from 1867, president of the Prussian House of Lords, and ambassador in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, and from 1878 to 1881 he was vice-chancellor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> under Bismarck.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-prince-of-stolberg-wernigerode.jpg" alt="Otto, Prince of Stolberg-Wernigerode" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Graf_Otto_zu_Stolberg-Wernigerode_1876.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
